  "notes": "やる is one of the most common verbs in casual Japanese, with two distinct meanings.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n\nSENSE 1 — TO DO (casual する):\n- ⟦{仕事|しごと}→仕事：00480_shigoto⟧をやる: to do work\n- ⟦{宿題|しゅくだい}→宿題：00812_shukudai⟧をやる: to do homework\n- やってみる: to give it a try\n- ⟦やり{直|なお}す→やり直す：03172_yarinaosu⟧: to redo\n- ⟦やり{遂|と}げる→やり遂げる：16745_yaritogeru⟧: to accomplish, to see through\n\nSENSE 2 — TO GIVE (downward):\nUsed for giving to animals, plants, or those of lower status:\n- ⟦{犬|いぬ}→犬：00632_inu⟧に⟦{餌|えさ}→餌：01886_esa⟧をやる: to feed the dog\n- ⟦{花|はな}→花：00523_hana⟧に⟦{水|みず}→水：02258_mizu⟧をやる: to water the flowers\n- ⟦{弟|おとうと}→弟：00572_otouto⟧に⟦{小遣|こづか}い→小遣い：12363_kozukai⟧をやる: to give one's younger brother pocket money\n\nWith people, sense 2 sounds blunt and can be rude if the listener is not clearly a social inferior or a close family junior. Many speakers now prefer ⟦あげる→あげる：00546_ageru⟧ even for children and pets.\n\nGIVING HIERARCHY:\n- やる: give (to animals/plants/inferiors — casual)\n- ⟦あげる→あげる：00546_ageru⟧: give (to equals — standard)\n- ⟦{差|さ}し{上|あ}げる→差し上げる：01597_sashiageru⟧: give (to superiors — humble/polite)\n\nREGISTER:\nやる (sense 1) is informal. In formal contexts, use ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ instead.",
